  "answer": "The official 2026 pricing policy (effective June 1, 2026) supersedes and raises rates above the deprecated 2025 proposal across all tiers, with higher monthly subscription fees and onboarding fees.\n\n- **Starter Plan** – 2026 monthly price increased from $900 to $1,200; onboarding fee increased from $1,500 to $2,500 [NL-004#NL-004-S05]. The deprecated 2025 proposal listed Starter at $900/month, $1,500 onboarding, 500 included learners, and 3 admin seats [NL-004#NL-004-S02].\n- **Growth Plan** – 2026 monthly price increased from $2,800 to $3,600; onboarding fee increased from $4,500 to $7,500 [NL-004#NL-004-S05]. The deprecated 2025 proposal listed Growth at $2,800/month, $4,500 onboarding, 2,000 included learners, and 10 admin seats [NL-004#NL-004-S02].\n- **Enterprise Plan** – 2026 starting monthly price increased from $6,000 to $8,500; onboarding fee increased from $10,000 to a minimum of $15,000 [NL-004#NL-004-S05]. The deprecated 2025 proposal listed Enterprise from $6,000/month with onboarding from $10,000 [NL-004#NL-004-S02].\n\nThe deprecated 2025 proposal is explicitly obsolete and rejected; all active sales, renewals, and negotiations must use the 2026 schedule [NL-004#NL-004-S01][NL-003#NL-003-S01][NL-004#NL-004-S02]. The 2026 schedule is the sole source of truth for pricing [NL-003#NL-003-S01].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
